    "explanation": "Both of you are asking about the same SGD 5.00 no-show fee on trip TRP-05064, charged at 15:49:04 and since refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver. What the record does show is the contact side: the driver sent two in-app messages (15:42:20 and 15:46:00) and placed one in-app call (15:45:10, unanswered, 25 s) before cancelling at 15:49:00, all on a COMPLETE chat log (EV-CHAT-05064, weight 1.0), so the POL-NS-23 obligation is met — the rider's own advocate does not dispute this. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-05064) shows exactly SGD 5.00, matching the POL-NS-22 figure. What the record cannot show is when, or whether, the driver was at the pickup. The no-show rules turn on the free wait, and for an on-demand trip with no scheduled time the free wait runs from the driver's arrival (POL-NS-21); this category's arrival test makes the driver 'at the pickup' only where the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace within 50 m. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05064) is impaired — weight 0.6, issue GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION — a 720-second gap from 15:38:00 to 15:50:00 that covers the 15:42:00 arrival marker, the whole waiting window and the 15:49:00 cancellation. Its derived arrival check returns corroborated = false with no nearest fix at all, and the fixes either side of the gap are several hundred metres from the pickup, so no reading before or after the gap places the driver there. The arrival limb is therefore undecided over exactly the stretch that matters, and an undecided limb supports neither a payment that needs the clause to hold (the driver's case for keeping the SGD 5.00 as compensation) nor a refund that needs it to fail (the rider's case that the fee be void). Neither a validly run-and-expired free wait nor a failure to arrive is established. Under POL-GEN-26, where a fact a rule needs — here, when the driver arrived — cannot be established because the evidence that would carry it is impaired, the case goes to a human reviewer and the amount is held. POL-NS-26 would make the AI's no-show ruling final below SGD 10.00, but it is expressly subject to POL-GEN-26, so it does not keep this case with the AI. On the driver's points: the trip record's 'cancelled_after_free_wait' derivation (EV-TRIP-05064) is computed from the driver's own arrival event, which the arrival test does not accept without GPS corroboration, so it cannot carry the finding; and the present refunded state cannot be converted into DRIVER_COMPENSATION when the charge's precondition is unproven. On the rider's points: the rider is right that the fee cannot be upheld on this record, but no corroborating GPS is not the same as a proven non-arrival, so the fee cannot be voided in the rider's favour either — hence escalation rather than a refund. The impaired artifact is named as POL-GEN-02(3) requires (EV-GPS-05064, weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION). Profiles were used only as POL-GEN-01 permits: both fraud_flags are 0, so no 0.95 bar arises, and no POL-NS-25 counter is present, so no referral arises; the SGD 5.00 fee equals the policy figure, so POL-NS-22 adds no referral. Confidence is 0.60, the weight of the sole artifact bearing on the undecided arrival fact. Open question for the reviewer: whether the driver was at Block 33, Jalan Bukit Merah at any point between 15:38:00 and 15:50:00 — the 720-second GPS gap over exactly that window leaves it unresolved, and the SGD 5.00 stays held pending that finding."
